# Backups
# `.backup` copies are written next to each data file by
# scripts/update-conditions.js as an in-run safety net before overwriting.
# They must never be committed: git history is already the backup, and
# tracking them rewrote ~17 MB across 186 files on every bot data commit
# (~15/day). Note `*.bak` alone did NOT match them — hence the explicit
# `*.backup`. (scripts/restore-data.js uses the separate `.backup/` dir.)
*.bak
*.backup
# `.tmp` sidecars from the atomic JSON writes (scripts/lib/atomicWriteJson.js):
# same rule as `.backup` above — and push-data-update.sh unstages `*.tmp`
# alongside `*.backup`, because that script commits with `git add -f`.
*.tmp

